      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The equitable distribution method for affordable housing units would depend on the specific needs of your city and its population. \n\nPrioritizing proximity to transit would target low-income residents who rely on public transportation, providing them with more accessible and affordable housing options. \n\nA housing lottery system based on income levels would ensure that those in need of assistance receive priority, regardless of transportation access. \n\nAlternatively, you could consider a mixed-methods approach, combining elements of both systems to cater to a variety of populations.",
